{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00118",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.19,
      "end_seconds": 4.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Good evening, doctor, thank you for staying late."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.91,
      "end_seconds": 7.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 8.27,
      "end_seconds": 12.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Doctor, um, I'm just here to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.17,
      "end_seconds": 15.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.44,
      "end_seconds": 22.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "Yeah, it's pain in my right ear. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.62,
      "end_seconds": 27.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.7,
      "end_seconds": 41.85,
      "duration_seconds": 14.15,
      "text": "A warm cloth helps a bit. I'd say mild. I've also had a blocked feeling in the ear, for about two weeks. Yeah, about blocked feeling in the ear, it's severe, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.64,
      "end_seconds": 46.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "What about a runny nose before it started, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.47,
      "end_seconds": 60.39,
      "duration_seconds": 10.92,
      "text": "Yeah, I've had that since last weekend. I've had a fever too, for about two weeks. As for fever, pretty moderate, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.91,
      "end_seconds": 66.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.87,
      "text": "Have you had any ringing, discharge from the ear, swelling behind the ear or recent swim?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.09,
      "end_seconds": 69.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Nothing like that, um, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.17,
      "end_seconds": 75.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Has there been any dizziness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.29,
      "end_seconds": 78.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any dizziness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 79.32,
      "end_seconds": 83.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice dizziness. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.18,
      "end_seconds": 90.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.28,
      "end_seconds": 99.04,
      "duration_seconds": 6.76,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.82,
      "end_seconds": 101.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "No, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.11,
      "end_seconds": 104.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.7,
      "end_seconds": 108.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "No, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.93,
      "end_seconds": 115.31,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.37,
      "end_seconds": 118.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "No, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.3,
      "end_seconds": 123.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.41,
      "end_seconds": 125.23,
      "duration_seconds": 0.82,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.78,
      "end_seconds": 143.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Okay, what about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.04,
      "end_seconds": 152.55,
      "duration_seconds": 8.51,
      "text": "I have asthma, for about a year. I've had migraines, yes. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.54,
      "end_seconds": 158.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Okay, migraines, that's already on your record. Good to know. Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.83,
      "end_seconds": 166.42,
      "duration_seconds": 6.59,
      "text": "Hmm, I had a knee arthroscopy three years ago. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.88,
      "end_seconds": 170.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "So, what medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.94,
      "end_seconds": 177.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.74,
      "text": "It's Seretide inhaler, twice a day for my asthma. Sumatriptan, 50 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 178.76,
      "end_seconds": 186.63,
      "duration_seconds": 7.87,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the sumatriptan was 25 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.5,
      "end_seconds": 191.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.63,
      "end_seconds": 201.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.76,
      "text": "Hmm, not with me. I'll bring it next time. I take paracetamol, 500 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.15,
      "end_seconds": 206.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.99,
      "end_seconds": 210.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "My father had a stroke. My mother has migraines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.74,
      "end_seconds": 214.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Let me know if I'm going too fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.5,
      "end_seconds": 216.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "No, you're fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.98,
      "end_seconds": 224.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.26,
      "end_seconds": 238.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Hold still for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.43,
      "end_seconds": 266.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "Okay: temp 38.9 degrees, heart rate 98, blood pressure 124 over 79, respiratory rate 19."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.23,
      "end_seconds": 268.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.2,
      "end_seconds": 272.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.06,
      "end_seconds": 277.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.25,
      "end_seconds": 281.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "A little pressure here, tell me if it's tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.67,
      "end_seconds": 297.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "The left ear looks normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.52,
      "end_seconds": 299.22,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.21,
      "end_seconds": 301.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "Let me press here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.9,
      "end_seconds": 311.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "The right eardrum looks red and bulging."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.3,
      "end_seconds": 338.46,
      "duration_seconds": 21.16,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. From what you've told me and what I found, I think we're dealing with a middle ear infection at this stage. I'd also keep an outer ear infection in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.76,
      "end_seconds": 341.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "Is it something serious, uh, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.13,
      "end_seconds": 355.31,
      "duration_seconds": 13.18,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like a middle ear infection. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had pain in your right ear, mild, and no discharge from the ear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 356.28,
      "end_seconds": 358.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 359.84,
      "end_seconds": 370.62,
      "duration_seconds": 10.78,
      "text": "I'd like you to take azithromycin, 500 milligrams, once a day, for three days. It's for ear infection. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 371.93,
      "end_seconds": 374.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Okay, and I take that after food?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.73,
      "end_seconds": 399.12,
      "duration_seconds": 23.39,
      "text": "Keep the ear dry for now and don't put anything in it, including cotton buds. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 399.84,
      "end_seconds": 401.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 402.39,
      "end_seconds": 411.3,
      "duration_seconds": 8.91,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if you get discharge, swelling behind the ear or the pain gets much worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 412.5,
      "end_seconds": 414.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 414.54,
      "end_seconds": 417.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Please come and see me in a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 418.82,
      "end_seconds": 419.52,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 420.17,
      "end_seconds": 424.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Just to confirm, what are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 425.13,
      "end_seconds": 432.52,
      "duration_seconds": 7.39,
      "text": "So, I take the azithromycin, 500 milligrams, once a day and come back in a week. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 433.78,
      "end_seconds": 439.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "Okay, yes, exactly right. Take care, and don't hesitate to call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 440.73,
      "end_seconds": 443.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Yeah, no questions. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 444.65,
      "end_seconds": 445.49,
      "duration_seconds": 0.84,
      "text": "Alright, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}